        "created_at": "2015-09-09T18:00:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I've tried searching the forums but can't quite find an exact answer. &nbsp;This would impact items like Amulet of the Elder Gods, Combat Stance, or Driving Mantis. &nbsp;What I'm trying to figure out is what happens if you take damage in a turn, play one of those cards, and then take damage again does this allow to use that reaction from those cards. &nbsp; The easiest scenario to setup would be Omnitron with Interpolation Beam and Wraith with Impromptu Invention and Combat Stance in hand. &nbsp; So Wraith plays Impromptu Invention, takes damage from card drawing due to Interpolation Beam, and then for the extra card play puts Combat Stance in play. &nbsp;The Wraith draws a card at end of turn and take damage due to Interpolation Beam. &nbsp;Should Wraith be able to deal damage to Omnitron due to Combat Stance? &nbsp; It is mostly a question of whether the card cares only about what happens after it enters play for \"first time\" or if it looks back at the whole turn it came into play for \"first time\".</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:24.341Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
