      {
        "id": 147388,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-10T14:57:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/100213#comment-100213\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">&nbsp;This thread</a> is pretty clear on tracking backwards, the linked post being the best summation.</p><p>Also this from the fireside chats:</p><blockquote><p><span>Driving Mantis only activates once per turn. What this means is that you only get one chance to say yes/no to redirecting damage to Mr. Fixer. For example, if Mr. Fixer will take 2 instances of damage in a turn, you cannot say NO to the first damage and YES to the second damage, as you have already missed your chance. Answering yes/no to the question uses it up. However, if you have a choice between Driving Mantis and Wrest The Mind, and you choose Wrest The Mind and redirect the damage, then Driving Mantis was never \"asked\" to be used, so it can still be used that turn.</span></p></blockquote><p><span>​They don't track backward, unless they are counting something, Combat Stance is not counting.</span></p><p>When Wraith takes the second damage you \"check\" Combat Stance to see if it has triggered that turn, if it hasn't, then it triggers.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:25:28.769Z",
