        "raw": "<p><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/100213#comment-100213\">&nbsp;This thread</a> is pretty clear on tracking backwards, the linked post being the best summation.</p><p>Also this from the fireside chats:</p><blockquote><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 21.6000003814697px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Driving Mantis only activates once per turn. What this means is that you only get one chance to say yes/no to redirecting damage to Mr. Fixer. For example, if Mr. Fixer will take 2 instances of damage in a turn, you cannot say NO to the first damage and YES to the second damage, as you have already missed your chance. Answering yes/no to the question uses it up. However, if you have a choice between Driving Mantis and Wrest The Mind, and you choose Wrest The Mind and redirect the damage, then Driving Mantis was never &quot;asked&quot; to be used, so it can still be used that turn.</span></p></blockquote><p><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Open Sans, HelveticaNeue, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 21.6000003814697px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">​They don&#39;t track backward, unless they are counting something, Combat Stance is not counting.</span></font></p><p>When Wraith takes the second damage you &quot;check&quot; Combat Stance to see if it has triggered that turn, if it hasn&#39;t, then it triggers.</p>",
